    "description": {
      "value": "You conjure a jagged lance of stone and then launch it at a foe. Make a spell attack roll against the target.\n\nOn a hit, you deal 6d6 piercing damage and the lance impales the creature, giving it a -10-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds unless it Escapes. On a critical hit, if the creature is on the ground, the lance also embeds into the ground and immobilizes the creature until it Escapes. A creature that Escapes after being impaled takes 3 persistent bleed damage. When the spell ends, the lance crumbles into dirt, freeing the target if it hasn't Escaped."
    },
    "higher_level_description": {
      "value": "Heightened (+1): Increase the damage by 2d6 and the persistent bleed damage for Escapes by 1."
    },
